<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Holstein-Pinneberg</h1><p class="st-meta">1290 CE – 1640 CE · capital Pinneberg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lower Elbe lordship of the Schauenburg counts, the last branch of Holstein's old rulers, who developed Altona and founded a university at Rinteln.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-schaumburg">Schauenburg</a> counts ruled <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> from 1111. When their lands were divided in 1290, one line kept the ancestral County of Schaumburg on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> together with the lordship of Pinneberg north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-hamburg">Hamburg</a>. This branch, known as Holstein-Schauenburg or Holstein-Pinneberg, survived after the main Holstein lines merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The counts ruled Pinneberg from a distance, with their main residence in Schaumburg at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stadthagen">Stadthagen</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buckeburg">Bückeburg</a>. Under them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altona">Altona</a> developed beside <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-hamburg">Hamburg</a> as a rival trading settlement. Count Ernest, raised to princely rank in 1619, founded a university at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rinteln">Rinteln</a> and built the court at Bückeburg. The family adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> in the 16th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The line died out with Count Otto V in 1640. Pinneberg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altona">Altona</a> passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and the dukes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">Holstein-Gottorp</a>, while Schaumburg was divided among <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Hesse-Kassel</a>, Lippe and Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1290 CE – 1640 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.37%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1290 CE – 1640 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pinneberg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ernest of Holstein-Schauenburg, Otto V of Holstein-Schauenburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Holstein-Schauenburg, Pinneberg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1465&amp;focus=county-of-holstein-pinneberg" aria-label="County of Holstein-Pinneberg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4898 334 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Holstein-Pinneberg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5218 590L5214 576M5218 590L5209 586"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5214 576h0M5209 586h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 590h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 590h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pinneberg. <a href="/atlas?year=1465&amp;focus=county-of-holstein-pinneberg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
